  "core_conclusions": [
    "Low-energy K1 orbital scissors tilts proton/neutron symmetry axes about a transverse direction; rotation about the common axial symmetry axis does not change density.",
    "Both modes use the same electromagnetic operator, but a universal low-1plus-to-MR branch conversion is not established by consulted evidence.",
    "Low-mode transition currents and blocked high-spin static currents are different density-matrix objects.",
    "Pair breaking and occupation changes require new self-consistent references; MR is not obtained by increasing one harmonic oscillation amplitude.",
    "Orbital/spin interference and upward/downward statistical factors are necessary before comparing strengths."
